From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sluongng <26684313+sluongng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:12:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] jj-core: Bound exact two-sided line comparisons

Remote annotation and local overlays need the same repeated-line choices
as ordinary jj annotation. A timeout around the eager histogram diff does
not stop its quadratic longest-common-subsequence work or recursive gap
processing, and a byte cap alone does not bound that work.

Add a separate two-sided literal line API with cumulative input, line,
work and conservative allocation budgets, bounded recursion and a caller
cancellation predicate. Check before allocation and during histogram
probes, LCS comparisons and gap traversal; return no partial diff after
exhaustion. Keep all existing entry points unchanged.

Use the same rare-token selection, LCS ties and leading/trailing fallback
as the existing implementation. Index shared tokens by source position
instead of sorting serial labels, preserving the identical permutation
while allowing cancellation during ordering. Bound allocations separately
from work and cap recursion at 128 frames even for permissive callers.
Allocation charges cover algorithm capacity, not borrowed input storage,
allocator metadata or process RSS; callers retain input/admission owners.

Test repeated lines, arbitrary bytes and newline boundaries against the
existing API, as well as pre-allocation rejection, cumulative quotas,
quadratic-work exhaustion and cancellation.
---
